# Everything the image build does NOT need. Without this the whole repo —
# including .git and 50+ KB of bilingual docs — is packed and sent to the
# daemon on every build, and any secret in a stray .env would land in the
# build context.
#
# Keep in mind: `docker build .` (the wordpress image) only needs the
# Dockerfile and mail/, while the backup image builds from ./backup.

.git
.github
.gitignore
.dockerignore

# Secrets and local state — must never enter a build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
docker-compose.override.yml
.verify/

# Docs (not needed inside the image)
*.md

# Local tooling
.claude/
.hadolint.yaml

# Runtime configs are bind-mounted at run time, not baked into the image.
apache/
mariadb/
php/
proxy-caddy/
ci/
verify.sh
init.sh
